The `.rho` files in this directory are vendored from rchain-community/rgov
(https://github.com/rchain-community/rgov), commit a045c181ec474fc1b9d8dda6221385340767e304,
`rholang/core/{Kudos,Inbox,Directory,memberIdGovRev,Issue}.rho` plus
`bootstrap/create-master-contract-directory-testnet.rho`, for use as node genesis content
(`spec/GENESIS.md`).

Licence: upstream declares `"license": "Apache-2.0"` in its `package.json`, but **ships no LICENSE
file** and GitHub reports no detectable licence for the repository. Apache-2.0 is the declared
intent, so these files are redistributed here under Apache-2.0; the upstream attribution above is
the required notice. If upstream adds a LICENSE file with different terms, this directory must be
re-checked before the next release. Recorded here rather than only in the commit message because the
licence situation is unusual and the next reader of these files will not have the commit in front of
them.

Local adaptations (all asserted at build time by `casper/src/genesis/standard_deploys.rs`, so a
change to a vendored file fails the build rather than shipping an unadapted copy):

- self-registration converted from `rho:registry:insertArbitrary` (whose URI is a hash of a random
  seed, so it shifts on every chain) to `rho:registry:insertSigned:secp256k1` (whose URI is a hash of
  the deployer public key — a constant, since genesis keys are fixed). This is what makes the URIs
  hardcodable, which is the point of installing these as genesis content.
- the *class* registration only: per-deployer registrations (a member directory's own write
  capability, an inbox instance's send capability) stay `insertArbitrary`, because they are runtime
  state, not classes.
- `memberIdGovRev.rho`'s two `match ("import", "./directory.rho", ...)` / `("./inbox.rho", ...)`
  markers are substituted with the vendored contracts' URIs.
- deploy-time **self-test traffic** is removed where upstream runs it at the end of the file
  (`Inbox.rho`'s trailing test program, `Directory.rho`'s post-registration exercise). A chain's
  genesis must not send test messages or print demo output. The class definitions themselves are
  untouched.
